"""
One valid, fully constructed sample of every dataclass defined by
`dumpex.output.records` and `dumpex.output.coverage`.

Each sample populates as many of its fields as the record's own validators
allow while staying small, and every value is a literal, so the sample set
depends on nothing outside this file. `tests/fixtures/
decomposition_baseline/record_corpus.py` serializes each sample and probes
every constructor field with invalid values; the committed golden records
the outcomes. Samples use the same synthetic values as the rest of the test
suite and never real case evidence.

Every name is imported from its legacy module path on purpose: a relocation
must keep each of these constructible through that path with the same field
names, defaults and validation.
"""
